WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.149
Film Courage: What are the key steps in developing
a web series?

00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:06.080
I know you’ve said before it’s not really
a film script so you can’t really divide

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.570
it up and just say great well these two pages
are going to be the first episode, you’ve

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:15.810
got to design it especially for that five
minute time period.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:22.829
Kathie Fong Yoneda: The most important thing
is that you have to have a character that

00:00:22.829 --> 00:00:29.679
you feel will hold the audiences interest
and he or she has to be involved in something

00:00:29.679 --> 00:00:32.230
that is relatable.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:40.480
So using something that is of personal interest
to the creator is probably one good way to

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.480
start.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.650
Start with an area of expertise that you’re
good at.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.460
There’s a guy named Ed and I’ve forgotten
his last name.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:54.650
But he had a web series and his was about
a guy who was a chef.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:01:03.700
And the guy…he could create great food,
with the women who just couldn’t do anything!

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:11.299
And what he did was start off with that premise
“What does a guy got to do?”

00:01:11.299 --> 00:01:21.159
And the fact that he eventually became a chef,
shows his trial and error of him eventually

00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:26.180
becoming a chef and eventually making contacts
and it’s very funny because one of his favorite

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:32.380
things is he goes to the same Sushi shop a
couple of times a week.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:35.899
And the real reason he goes is not just because
he likes the Sushi but he has a crush on this

00:01:35.899 --> 00:01:46.359
one gal who works there and unfortunately
he sees this Asian guy come in giving the

00:01:46.359 --> 00:01:50.149
gal a hug and everything and saying all of
this and I missed you and everything.

00:01:50.149 --> 00:01:54.079
And so he thinks “Oh my gosh, she’s got
a husband or a boyfriend.”

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:55.859
And she’s interested in him too.

00:01:55.859 --> 00:01:59.869
And she flirts with him and always asking
him “How are you doing?”

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:00.869
It’s really cute.

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:09.220
And it turns out by the end of the first season
(I think the last episode) he finds out that

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:14.030
that’s her brother!

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:19.620
And then the love interest grows from that.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:26.790
But it’s starting off with something maybe
an area that you know about like in his case

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:35.110
it was called, his web series is called PAIRINGS.

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:39.349
And you usually think of pairings as ‘Okay
what wine goes with this kind of dinner’

00:02:39.349 --> 00:02:40.459
or whatever?

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:48.140
But it’s a play on words about what is was
like for this poor guy who’s a good cook

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:52.890
but just can’t see…he can cook everything
and anything but he just can’t seem to get

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:53.890
a gal.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:57.790
Film Courage: But did he take this from his
own experience?

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:59.310
Was he or is he a chef?

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.310
Kathie: Yes.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:12.560
And in fact he uses that as way to advertise
what he does is he’ll say “If you subscribe

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.939
to our web series” (and it doesn’t cost
anything to subscribe.

00:03:15.939 --> 00:03:23.450
In his case it didn’t, you’ll get this
week’s recipes.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:31.379
It’s something a little different which
kind of makes it interesting for the viewer

00:03:31.379 --> 00:03:33.459
and the fans.

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:41.840
And as it turns out this guy (I think) is
going to be doing a cookbook.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:54.090
And there is also an Olive Oil company I believe
and a winery that advertised now so he kind

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:57.349
of got sponsors from it.

00:03:57.349 --> 00:04:00.379
So he didn’t purposely go out to do that.

00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:05.099
When we were talking a little bit about “Well
I have to find a sponsor first.”

00:04:05.099 --> 00:04:07.650
In this case the sponsor found him.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:14.439
Film Courage: So built it and sort of that
Field of Dreams analogy but don’t set out

00:04:14.439 --> 00:04:16.229
to have it be your only goal.

00:04:16.229 --> 00:04:17.739
Kathie: And they’ll come.

00:04:17.739 --> 00:04:25.060
Well if you don’t have the story, in his
case he was just fascinated by web series

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:32.370
and he always enjoyed writing and telling
stories and so for him to do that and his

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:38.580
day job was being a chef and he combined the
two of them.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:43.460
And so there are no “Okay, first you do
this, this and this.”

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:46.840
It’s hard, it’s the same as any kind of
writing.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:50.720
You’ve got to sit down, put your butt in
the chair and do it.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:54.030
That’s the first step.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:05:00.910
Most of the successful web series I’ve seen
a lot of them started off by taking a character

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:09.599
not unlike sometimes themselves and trying
to see Okay what’s the surrounding?

00:05:09.599 --> 00:05:13.319
What’s the environment?

00:05:13.319 --> 00:05:18.230
Another friend of mine did one, she’s lesbian.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:23.800
And she noticed that there weren’t any lesbian
web series and she wanted to talk about the

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:31.410
fact that a lot of people don’t understand
that really that no matter what your sexuality

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:38.110
is people have stories and they have the same
fears and insecurities that all of go through

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:39.910
when we’re in a relationship.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:46.040
And so she did one and it’s in Australia
and it’s called STARTING FROM NOW and it’s

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:47.630
becoming an Internet sensation.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:52.250
They have fans all over the world and they
won a lot of awards.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:58.699
But she took the world that she was in and
she thought how can I do something that’s

00:05:58.699 --> 00:06:05.160
going to be interesting and have characters
that I think people are going to care about.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:10.870
And when you look at it those characters,
they worry about their job just like we do,

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:17.080
they worry about what their families are going
to think just like we do, they worry about

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:23.020
what the political situations are like or
they worry about people cheating on them.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:27.000
And you see all of those things playing out.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:31.349
They are now finishing up (I think they may
have finished up) by now their fifth season,

00:06:31.349 --> 00:06:33.750
so they’ve done incredibly well.

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:36.259
Film Courage: What’s the name of it again?

00:06:36.259 --> 00:06:41.220
Kathie: STARTING FROM NOW and it’s based
in Australia but you can see it here, I mean

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:42.520
you can just Google it and it will come up.

